  "id": "Compound::DB00671 - Gene::6565",
  "verbalization": "Cefixime, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, exhibits a strong binding interaction with Slc15a1, a gene that is involved in the transport of oligopeptides and peptides across cellular membranes. This binding is consistent across three distinct paths, each showing that Slc15a1 participates in different transport activities, including proton-dependent peptide transport and oligopeptide transporter functions. These pathways ultimately lead to Slc15a2, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Cefixime influences the expression or function of Slc15a2. The shared binding of Cefixime to Slc15a1 and its involvement in multiple transport processes imply that it may modulate the activity of Slc15a2 through a common pathway, possibly by interfering with the transport of peptides or oligopeptides across cellular membranes. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Cefixime and Slc15a2, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
